This room runs nearly the entire length of this floor, but its size only draws attention to its emptiness. The walls are bare plaster; what little furniture remains is stacked in the corners and covered with dusty sheets.

You can't help but imagine how this place once was, in its full vibrancy. The cream of the city once filled this room, entertained and served by the Duke of Toresal — your father. They respected him, honored him, even loved him. And now it's all gone.

A wide stairway sweeps up to the second floor, while a narrower stairway leads down to a cellar. The foyer lies south. {portrait-on-the-wall}
